    "title": "Donation to bring science and technology to Ohio second grade - NewsBreak",
    "text": "11 hours ago\nSCIOTO COUNTY, Ohio (WOWK) - A donation aims to bring in more science and technology to the classroom to get students excited about learning.\nThe second-grade class at Valley Elementary School has received more than $1,000 to provide unique learning opportunities in Science, Technology, Engineering and Math.\n“Any opportunity to incorporate hands-on learning is a good way to stimulate learning,” said Southern Ohio Cleanup Company President and CEO, Pat Timbes. “Valley is also a part of our STEAM Ahead program that provides hands-on learning to third graders, so the experience for these students will continue into next year.”\nA teacher at Valley Elementary says that they hope to bring COSI on Wheels to the school for the students. The teachers also hope to provide more science literature to the classrooms through books and technology.\nThis project will serve 100 second graders.\nFor more news from across the Tri-State, click here .\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WOWK 13 News.",
    "summary": "SCIOTO COUNTY, Ohio (WOWK) - A donation aims to bring in more science and technology to the classroom to get students excited about learning. The second-grade class at Valley Elementary School has received more than $1,000 to provide unique learning opportunities in Science, Technology, Engineering and Math. “Any opportunity to incorporate hands-on learning is a good way to stimulate learning,” said Southern Ohio Cleanup Company President and CEO, Pat Timbes.",
